{
 "about": "Kingdom rebuilt the way the platform builds games: ten small graphs, each on the thing it is about and started by events; nothing compares positions on a timer. State is in custom variables of the player (coins, citizens, builders, archers, keep, night) and of the things themselves (a wall's hp, the site's level, whether the bow shop is loaded). Stations are prefabs with an option tab: walk up, press F. Coins are prefabs with a follow device and two collision triggers. The stage graph only keeps the clock: dusk, the wave, dawn, income, victory. Walls count the Greed that reach them through a collision trigger for creatures; the bow shop shoots one Greed that enters its range and reloads; a Greed that gets near the monarch takes a coin through its own collision trigger for characters, or the crown from an empty purse. Signals: KG_dawn (walls are mended, the Greed leave, the bow shop reloads), KG_wall_down (the Greed turn to the monarch, the site can be built on again). Prints, in the order the script below should produce them: KG_READY, KG_DAY, KG_COINS 10, KG_CITIZEN x2, KG_BUILDER, KG_ARCHER, KG_WALL 1, KG_DUSK, KG_GREED x2, KG_SHOT, KG_WALL_HIT, KG_DAWN, KG_MENDED, KG_GREED_GONE if any is left, KG_INCOME 3, KG_COINS up to 3, KG_DUSK, KG_GREED x3, KG_DAWN, KG_VICTORY. KG_POOR / KG_NEED mean a station refused. Screenshots: price tags (small coins) above the stations, the purse bar, the clock, villagers appearing, the wall, the dark sky with lamps, Greed running at the wall. Played to the official victory screen on 2026-10-10 and 11: each night the Greed run at the wall, the bow shop shoots one that comes in range (KG_SHOT) and reloads, the next one reaches the wall (KG_WALL_HIT). Night and day are two skies made with scene_add_environment; three lamps belong to the night one. The level's graphs start about five seconds before the scripted inputs do, so dusk falls about 26 seconds into the script and dawn about 52.",
